  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "mC1hcSRZPBU57ILgqnPlSIvaVtA=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:32.854Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "GFT Technologies SE holds Camunda Platinum status twice over \u2014 through its Italian and Polish organisations \u2014 and also appears as a Flowable partner. Platinum is the top certification tier, and holding it in two delivery countries at once is the strongest Camunda credential in the sweep.\n\nThat credential is also what defines the obstacle. A listed enterprise in financial services, delivering from Stuttgart with Italian and Polish delivery centres, buys new technology through a committee: alliance management scores it against existing partner commitments, architecture review governs the reference stack, and Platinum status itself creates an obligation to the incumbent vendor. The record's own summary is committee sale, and that is what holds the row at priority 3 rather than any doubt about capability.\n\nThe entity split is worth carrying separately. GFT's UK arm appears elsewhere in the same corpus filed at priority 9 on banking-only positioning aimed at tier-1 banks, with its stack never researched. Same group, two rows, two verdicts nine priority points apart \u2014 the assessments are entity-level, and neither row closes the other. Provenance: Flowable Partner Finder, mined 2026-08-18, not imprint-swept.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- GFT Technologies SE (DE Stuttgart + IT/PL delivery) \u2014 gft.com\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> DUAL: Camunda Platinum x2 (Italia + Poland). Listed enterprise, financial services. Committee sale \u00b7 SOURCE: Flowable Partner Finder (flowable.com/company/partners), mined 2026-08-18. NOT imprint-swept.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:32:32.854717Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:32.854722Z"
    }
  },
